Symfony is a high‑performance, open‑source PHP framework for building web applications and APIs.  It follows the MVC (Model‑View‑Controller) pattern, provides a rich set of reusable components (routing, dependency injection, form handling, security, etc.), and encourages best‑practice development through conventions, configuration, and a powerful bundle system.  Backed by a vibrant community and long‑term support releases, Symfony scales from small projects to enterprise‑grade solutions.
